          "title": "You'll want to know: el titular",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el titular — \"the headline\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El titular habla del accidente. The headline is about the accident."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Los titulares are the headlines. As an adjective, titular means holding a post: el profesor titular."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "titular comes from Late Latin titulāre 'to give a title to' (EtymDB), built on titulus 'an inscription, a label' (Lewis & Short), the word behind título. A headline is the title printed over a story."
            }
          ]
        },
